# udev rule: stable name for the goalkeeper Arduino regardless of ttyUSB/ttyACM
# numbering. Your board is a CH340 (from `lsusb`: 1a86:7523), so it enumerates
# as /dev/ttyUSB0 (NOT ttyACM0). This rule makes it always reachable at:
#
#     /dev/goalkeeper_serial
#
# These IDs are already filled in for your board (1a86:7523). If you ever swap
# to a different board, re-check with `lsusb` and update idVendor/idProduct.

SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7523", SYMLINK+="goalkeeper_serial", MODE="0666"
